{"title":"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) #19</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) #21</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A bicycle at Store P costs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/0/4a0d1ea2f817036d72f6d1449562fc3a1dfd01da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" />. The regular price of the same bicycle at Store Q is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/a/87a8787ca8fcdf64f42e938d20fa64f63871646d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> more than it is at Store P. The bicycle is on sale at Store Q for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/5/2b56bd637cb2c936d539be1b5000a64a898af389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> off of the regular price. What is the sale price of the bicycle at Store Q?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/c/efceed3ab4d2d07242fb93d92e2c0e150185a937.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\$230.00 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\$201.50 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\$199.00 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\$207.00 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\$210.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"604\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we can find the regular price of the bicycle at Store Q. Then, we can figure out the sale price from that regular price.\n</p><p>Since the bicycle costs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/6/746c6f43a871baa67e9541969f340d4296d48ffb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$200.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" /> at Store P and costs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/a/87a8787ca8fcdf64f42e938d20fa64f63871646d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> more at Store Q than it does at Store P, the regular price of the bicycle at Store Q is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/6/d562616550cade7a7ad4c6b7dd9aec3b81e554d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$200.00 + \\$200.00 \\times 15\\% = \\$200 \\times 1.15 = \\$230.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"398\" height=\"17\" /> \n</p><p>Next, the sales price is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/5/2b56bd637cb2c936d539be1b5000a64a898af389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> off this regular price at Store Q. We then have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/b/37be3f28be5c41dac8585c49e0a0bfc82ffdcb45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$230.00 - \\$230.00 \\times 10\\% = \\$230.00 - \\$23.00 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } \\$207.00}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"486\" height=\"31\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=